        "original_id": "2543ff7d-5a09-5fdb-8dad-ce60427d0607",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Simon Helberg, Jeremy Konner, Jason Ritter, Jocelyn Towne\n- Music Groups: Army Navy\n- Albums and Songs: The Last Place, Ode to Janice Melt\n- Television and Films: The Big Bang Theory, We'll Never Have Paris\n- Awards: Critics' Choice Television Award\n- Organizations: The Fever Zone\n\nFacts:\n- Simon Helberg was born on December 9, 1980, and he is an American actor, comedian, and musician.\n- Simon Helberg became best known for playing Howard Wolowitz in the sitcom The Big Bang Theory, which began in 2007.\n- Army Navy released its second studio album, The Last Place, on July 12, 2011, on the band's own label, The Fever Zone.\n- A music video for Army Navy's song Ode to Janice Melt was released on September 15, 2011.\n- Jeremy Konner directed the Ode to Janice Melt music video, and Jason Ritter and Simon Helberg starred in it.\n- Simon Helberg won a Critics' Choice Television Award in 2013 for his work on The Big Bang Theory.\n- We'll Never Have Paris is a 2014 American romantic comedy directed by Simon Helberg in his directorial debut and by Jocelyn Towne.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
